\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Source probability laws. Columns of panels distinguish datasets; panel rows distinguish the image-derived and confounded regimes. Within a panel, each row is one source and each column is a frozen prediction cell. The shared color mapping runs from probability zero to one.}}{18}{figure.3.1}%
